{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1372895-errata-for-secrets-of-the-covenants","id":1372895,"title":"errata for Secrets of the covenants?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-04T21:40:19-08:00","id":1372895,"title":"errata for Secrets of the covenants?","content":"I know Onyx Path doesn't do official errata or faqs, so I was wondering if anyone had some unofficial errata for Secrets of the Covenants. The more I look through the appendices the more I wonder if this book was ever playtested. I mean the Zirnitra Coil should just not have been allowed to be a thing, and who actually thought the instant death black hole part of the Opening the Void Cruac Style was a good thing. It's gotten to the point where I'm considering banning this book outright from all of my chronicles. I mean CoD isn't the greatest when it comes to balance (professional training, for example), but this book just goes above and beyond. So, has anyone actually managed to fix this book, or would it just be better to ban certain sections, or even the whole thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T03:52:56-08:00","id":1372930,"title":"","content":"Professional Training was included because of how well received it was in Hunter 1e. It does wonders to make characters stand out in their chosen field. The only thing we've done to balance it is to remove 9-Again and Rote Action from attack rolls because otherwise not choosing your main combat Skill as one of the Asset Skills would seriously unbalance the party in combat heavy games. Other than that my only problem with PT is that its effects aren't baked into character creation. Kinda sucks that you'll always want to put 3-5 of your starting Merit dots into PT.<br /> <br /> Coil of Zirnitra on its own isn't that powerful. You get Supernatural Merits that generally aren't better than Disciplines but they cost huge amounts of XP <b>and</b> it says directly that all Supernatural Merits needs to be discussed and judged on an individual basis. Just don't allow Pyrokinesis and the Coil is absolutely fine. Grafting Unholy Flesh, on the other hand, is a powergamer's wet dream and should definitely be banned if you're worried about balance.<br /> <br /> Other than that single Scale, Coil of Ziva is the worst offender. Unlike Zirnitra (and its Scales, I might add) this was immediately banned at our table. It's also a horrible mess of mechanics so if you for whatever reason don't find it too unbalanced I'd recommend checking out the rewrite in my forum signature.<br /> <br /> Just remove the oblivion gate from Opening the Void and it should work fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can't think of anything else that is unbalanced in that direction. The Crusade Style in the LeS section is close to worthless against blood sorcery (which it is supposed to counter) because you'd never want to cast blood sorcery while in combat anyway. The second dot works well against uses of Dominate and possibly Majesty in combat, but that's basically it outside of crossover games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T04:24:03-08:00","id":1372932,"title":"","content":"Agreed with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13542\" data-vbnamecard=\"13542\">Shadowdragon</a> I know other people have errata'd or attempted to fix the Coil of Ziva, so by any means you should check their work out too, but here is my attempt at fixing the Coil of Ziva without changing too much. I'll see if I can fix Coil of Zirnitra as well (though I feel that Coil doesn't need as much fixing, it just needs a firm ST who doesn't allow power gaming to say &quot;no&quot; when a player with that Coil tries to pull off a game-breaking combo like Pyrokinesis).<br /> <br /> My take on Coil of Ziva:<br /> <br /> <b><i><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Coil of Ziva</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Denying the Bane \u2022</span></b></i></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">At this initial level, the character may shrug off some of the more heinous effects of her degeneration. Add her Coil dots to her Humanity for the purpose of determining the effects of her Banes. This includes her clan Bane, acquired Banes and bloodline Banes. This does not, however, affect the vampire\u2019s weaknesses to fire or sunlight. This also doesn\u2019t affect the Ventrue clan Bane. The Mekhet's Tenebrous Curse caps their effective maximum Humanity at 9 even if this Coil would push it above nine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>Enliven the Anima \u2022\u2022</b></span></span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>With this Coil, your character becomes resistant to the psychological strains of encountering Breaking Points. She finds overcoming her soul\u2019s trials invigorating. Any time she succeeds a Detachment roll and doesn't already have the Raptured Condition, you may choose to take the Raptured Condition instead of Bestial, Competitive or Wanton.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Buttress the Soul \u2022\u2022\u2022</b></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">When facing a Breaking Point, the Dragon may now choose to spend Willpower on the resulting Detachment roll. This works similarly to spending Willpower on resisting frenzy. Each point of Willpower spent adds a +1 die bonus to the Detachment roll.</span></span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Embracing the Banes \u2022\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Your character can sustain a number of acquired Banes equal to her dots in the Coil of Ziva (instead of three) and her acquired banes no longer inflict a die penalty on her Detachment rolls.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The player may choose to acquire a Bane for a particular breaking point even when succeeding the Detachment roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Siphon the Soul \u2022\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022\u2022</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">This ability acts as a sort of pseudo-Amaranth which can be used on humans and vampires with an Integrity/Humanity rating higher than the character's own Humanity rating. The vampire drains a human or Kindred victim completely and then continues to do so further. She spends Willpower and rolls Strength + Resolve as she normally would when committing diablerie (see Vampire: The Requiem, Second Edition p. 101).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">When the victim dies, the vampire gains a dot of Humanity, but also rolls for Detachment for premeditated murder (Humanity 2), possibly losing the stolen Humanity dot, and suffers the Tainted Condition. While under the effects of the Tainted Condition, the user of this Coil might register as a diablerist to Auspex users.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The vampire can end there, or choose to complete the Amaranth if the victim is Kindred, with all the consequences of doing so (this counts as a separate breaking point at Humanity 1).</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><i>Scales of Ziva</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin</b></span></i></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><b>Prerequisite Coil:</b> Siphon the Soul<br /> <b>Procedure:</b> The vampire distills a bit of her own Humanity into a decoction that can turn any vampire into a human again, for a brief time at least. Preparing the decoction takes a full hour and costs the vampire one Vitae and one Humanity dot. This Humanity loss is unavoidable and cannot be shielded with a Bane. The end result is a decoction in a vial or syringe, that can be consumed or injected by a vampire to briefly turn human again.<br /> <b>Outcome: </b>The vampire who receives the decoction undergoes rapid changes. His blood starts to boil, his skin starts to burn, flake and fall off. The Beast goes berserk and the vampire has to roll to resist frenzy with a -5 die penalty. This whole transformation process takes 5 turns, during which the Beast cries out in agony and the vampire turns human again. After these 5 turns, the vampire passes out, but will soon wake up, breathing, with a beating heart and completely human in every single way. No doctor in the world could see him as anything but human. This also means all Disciplines, Vitae, Banes and everything that made the character vampire disappears for the time being. The character's Humanity rating becomes his Integrity rating for the time being.<br /> While human, the character can engage in sexual intercourse and possibly impregnate or get impregnated, but such a pregnancy is unlikely to produce a normal, healthy human. A dhampir on the other hand...<br /> The character stays human until the next sundown. During sundown, for nearly a half an hour, she suffers agonizing pain as she slowly dies. This leaves her functionally incapacitated during this time. This might inflict a breaking point after the fact. When the character is completely dead, she will immediately wake up as her former Kindred self, being one of the unliving once again. She can hold off the transformation for one minute with a point of Willpower. Once she\u2019s changed back, roll one die to determine her new starting Vitae.</i></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","user":"Tomorrow's Nobody","date":". 03-05-2020, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T05:17:19-08:00","id":1372942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1372895-errata-for-secrets-of-the-covenants?p=1372930#post1372930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Professional Training was included because of how well received it was in Hunter 1e. It does wonders to make characters stand out in their chosen field. The only thing we've done to balance it is to remove 9-Again and Rote Action from attack rolls because otherwise not choosing your main combat Skill as one of the Asset Skills would seriously unbalance the party in combat heavy games. Other than that my only problem with PT is that its effects aren't baked into character creation. Kinda sucks that you'll always want to put 3-5 of your starting Merit dots into PT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it, if you make a new one-dot merit that gives you 9-again on a mundane skill roll, you could accomplish the same thing as PT by just giving your characters 4-5 extra mundane experience at character creation. The fifth dot of PT is not really worth taking or converting to a merit. I think that's probably what I'll do in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 03-05-2020, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T07:47:36-08:00","id":1372966,"title":"","content":"If 9-Again is the only thing you want, sure, but I think the extra Specialties and Contacts does quite a lot for bringing the character concept to life even if they're not used in the game. And strong disagree on the fifth dot. Rote Action beats +3 dice on Asset Skill rolls where your base dice pool is four dice or higher. The higher the dice pool, the better Rote Action becomes. If you add Specialties and equipment modifiers you'll soon reach the point where Rote Action will bring you Exceptional Success more often than not.<br /> <br /> But this is all pretty subjective and you do what you think works best at your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T09:34:05-08:00","id":1372988,"title":"","content":"A question and a comment:<br /> Question: I thought that dice tricks don't stack. That is, you can't combine 8-again or 9-again with rote action. Is that a 1e thing or did my brain just completely make that up?<br /> <br /> Comment: I totally agree with the contacts and specialties, I was just pointing out that, two contacts is worth 2 xp, 9-again on three skills is worth about 3 merit dots (3 xp), two specialties is worth 2 xp, a skill dot is worth 2 xp, and I don't know how to value trading 3 dice for rote-action. Even if you think it's worth, say, 3 merit dots (3xp) to be able to do that, that gives you a combined total of 12 xp worth of benefits for a 5-dot (5xp) merit. I would much rather just give my players an extra 12-5=7 xp/merit dots at character creation for mundane purposes and let them customize their character further.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I strongly agreed with your comment here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other than that my only problem with PT is that its effects aren't baked into character creation. </div> </div> </div>There's already a perfectly good system for customizing characters. PT is something every character takes anyway, might as well just calculate its net value and let players have more control over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T09:57:13-08:00","id":1372991,"title":"","content":"Dice tricks stacks. You can have Rote Action, 9/8-Again and even Advanced Action on the same roll.<br /> Multiple sources of 9-Again does not stack to 8-Again unless one of those sources explicitly says so (like this: &quot;if you already have 9-Again from another source, you instead get 8-Again&quot;).<br /> <br /> I've seen arguments based ln the phrasing of Rote Action that you wouldn't even roll the regular 10-Again, but that's overly literal bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T10:25:40-08:00","id":1372999,"title":"","content":"Well, dang. If you're allowed to stack 9-again or 8-again then it's much more worth it. 7 dice with 8-again+rote would actually be ~50% chance of exceptional success (or 8 dice with 9-again+rote). I agree that this makes it actually useful, but only if you want to go for an exceptional success. Getting any success at all is marginally improved vs just adding 3 dice.<br /> <br /> And all of that to say, I think it would still make more sense to just be a merit and let players buy it a-la-carte instead of creating a convoluted merit track for it. :P<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T20:53:20-07:00","id":1373837,"title":"","content":"Like Shedding The Beasts Skin as a Scale.<br /> <br /> That way its something Kindred Can seek out an elusive master that can grant it to them for a boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-11-2020, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}